/T (One of the most compelling aspects of the novel is its exploration of the nature of regret. Through Nora's journey, readers are prompted to consider their own regrets and the ways in which they shape our lives. The book challenges the notion of a "perfect" life and encourages acceptance of one's choices, however imperfect they may seem. "The Midnight Library" also delves into the concept of parallel universes and the idea that every choice we make creates a new reality. )
